content:
{
  "query": "What are the active requirements for team introduction, member cards and profile content (including photos, interests, fun facts, AI opinions and hot takes), shared future-of-software-engineering content, and current footer?",
  "results": [
    {
      "source": "SG-35",
      "text": "# SG-35: Page structure Status: ACTIVE (version 2) Category: Structure A team website consists of these parts, in this order: 1. `<header>` with the group name, tagline and theme toggle 2. `<main>` containing: - `<section id=\"team\">` – the team introduction and all member cards - `<section id=\"future-of-se\">` – the team's shared view on AI and the future of software engineering, with the heading \"The Future of Software Engineering\" 3. `<footer>`, see the current footer document The section ids are used for navigation links and MUST be exactly as given. Additional sections (for example a \"fun statistics\" section) MAY be added between the two required sections."
    },
    {
      "source": "SG-30",
      "text": "# SG-30: Member cards Status: ACTIVE (version 2) Category: Components Every team member is introduced in exactly one member card. ## Markup - Each card MUST be an `<article>` element with the class `member-card`. - There MUST be exactly one member card per team member. No placeholder cards. - Cards are placed inside the team section, see the page structure document. - Cards are ordered alphabetically by first name. ## Content of a card, in this order 1. Photo (see the member photos document) 2. Name as an `h3` 3. Study background in one line 4. Bio (see the bio writing document) 5. Hot take badge (see the hot take badge document)"
    },
    {
      "source": "SG-34",
      "text": "# SG-34: Team introduction Status: ACTIVE Category: Content The team section starts with a short introduction of the whole group. - Two to four sentences: who you are as a group and what connects you. - You MAY include a team motto. - Mention the lab (\"Agentic Software Engineering, Paderborn University\")."
    },
    {
      "source": "SG-33",
      "text": "# SG-33: Member photos Status: ACTIVE Category: Components - Each member card contains one `<img>` with a photo, avatar or drawing of the member. - Every image MUST have a meaningful `alt` text in the format \"Photo of <first name>\" (or \"Avatar of <first name>\"). Empty alt texts are not allowed. - Images are embedded as data URIs, see the single-file delivery document. - Photos are displayed as circles with a size of `8rem` × `8rem` and `object-fit: cover`. - Members who don't want to show a photo use an avatar. This is always fine."
    },
    {
      "source": "SG-08",
      "text": "# SG-08: Writing member bios Status: ACTIVE Category: Content Each member card contains a short bio. - Length: 60 to 120 words. - Written in the third person (\"Anna studies ...\"), not the first person. - Mention: study background, one or two interests, one fun fact. - Mention one thing the member thinks about AI in software engineering today. - Don't include private data such as phone numbers, addresses or birthdays."
    }
  ],
  "total_tokens": 594
}

