content:
{
  "query": "What are the active rules for day/night themes and theme toggle, responsive layout, reduced motion, hot take badges, single-file image delivery, navigation, and footer content?",
  "results": [
    {
      "source": "SG-23",
      "text": "# SG-23: Images in night mode Status: ACTIVE Category: Theming Bright photos can be uncomfortable in night mode. - In night mode, photos SHOULD be shown with `filter: brightness(0.9)`. - Don't invert photos or apply other color filters."
    },
    {
      "source": "SG-57",
      "text": "# SG-57: Print styles Status: ACTIVE Category: Structure Print styles are optional. - If provided, hide the theme toggle when printing. - Print always in day mode colors."
    },
    {
      "source": "SG-22",
      "text": "# SG-22: Theme toggle control Status: ACTIVE Category: Theming - The toggle MUST be a `<button>` element with the id `theme-toggle`. - It MUST have an `aria-label` describing the action, for example `aria-label=\"Switch to night mode\"`. Update the label when the theme changes. - It SHOULD show a sun symbol in night mode and a moon symbol in day mode. - It SHOULD be placed in the top right corner of the header. - Don't use a checkbox for the toggle."
    },
    {
      "source": "SG-20",
      "text": "# SG-20: Theme switching mechanics Status: ACTIVE Category: Theming The theme is controlled by one attribute on the root element. - The `<html>` element MUST carry the attribute `data-theme` with the value `light` or `dark`. - JavaScript switches the theme by changing this attribute, not by toggling classes on the body. - The CSS MUST define the colors for each theme with attribute selectors, for example `[data-theme=\"light\"] { ... }` and `[data-theme=\"dark\"] { ... }`. - Components use CSS custom properties (for example `var(--bg)`), so they don't need theme-specific rules."
    },
    {
      "source": "SG-58",
      "text": "# SG-58: Review checklist Status: ACTIVE Category: Meta Before submitting, go through this list: - [ ] Title and language set as described in the metadata document - [ ] Current day and night palettes used (not the deprecated ones) - [ ] Accent color defined as a custom property - [ ] Theme switching and persistence implemented as described in the theming documents - [ ] Toggle is an accessible button - [ ] One member card per member, each with a hot take badge - [ ] Photos have alt texts - [ ] Required sections with the correct ids - [ ] Exactly one h1 - [ ] Current footer text - [ ] Current breakpoint - [ ] System font, rem font sizes - [ ] Reduced motion respected"
    }
  ],
  "total_tokens": 478
}

