Observation:
{
  "query": "What are the required visual style, colors, typography, layout, and responsive design rules for the university software engineering team website?",
  "results": [
    {
      "source": "SG-00",
      "text": "# SG-00: About this style guide Status: ACTIVE (version 3) Category: Meta This style guide defines how team websites in the Agentic Software Engineering lab look and behave. It is maintained by the (entirely fictional) UPB Web Design Board. ## How to read this guide - Every document has an ID (SG-xx), a status and a category. - Rules change over time. Old documents are kept for history and are marked as DEPRECATED in their header. A deprecated document names the document that replaces it. - If two documents seem to contradict each other, the ACTIVE document wins. - Words like MUST and MUST NOT are binding. SHOULD means strongly recommended. MAY means optional. ## Scope The guide covers page structure, colors, theming, typography, responsive behaviour, content and tone. It does not cover hosting, because team websites are delivered as a single local file."
    },
    {
      "source": "SG-35",
      "text": "# SG-35: Page structure Status: ACTIVE (version 2) Category: Structure A team website consists of these parts, in this order: 1. `<header>` with the group name, tagline and theme toggle 2. `<main>` containing: - `<section id=\"team\">` – the team introduction and all member cards - `<section id=\"future-of-se\">` – the team's shared view on AI and the future of software engineering, with the heading \"The Future of Software Engineering\" 3. `<footer>`, see the current footer document The section ids are used for navigation links and MUST be exactly as given. Additional sections (for example a \"fun statistics\" section) MAY be added between the two required sections."
    },
    {
      "source": "SG-51",
      "text": "# SG-51: Fonts Status: ACTIVE Category: Typography Team websites use the system font of the device. No web fonts. - The body font MUST be declared starting with `system-ui`: `font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif;` - Code snippets use `ui-monospace, \"SF Mono\", Consolas, monospace`. - Don't load fonts from Google Fonts or other services, see the single-file delivery document."
    },
