          <p class="bio">Aniket is pursuing an M.Sc. in Computer Science at Paderborn University after earning a bachelor's degree in Computer Engineering from Savitribai Phule Pune University. He enjoys travelling and cooking, alongside a long list of creative and active pursuits. A theatre skit once earned him an award at an Asia-level national competition. Aniket sees AI as a useful assistant for coding, debugging and learning, but believes developers must understand and verify its output rather than depend on it blindly.</p>
          <p class="hot-take">🔥 Developers who use AI effectively may replace those who don't.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img class="member-photo" src="{{image:dheeraj.jpg}}" alt="Photo of Dheeraj">
          <h3>Dheeraj</h3>
          <p class="study-line">M.Sc. Computer Science, 1st semester · Paderborn University</p>
          <p class="bio">Dheeraj is a first-semester M.Sc. Computer Science student at Paderborn University, following a B.Tech in Computer Science and Engineering at Anurag University. Software development, gaming and anime are among his interests, and he also makes time for fitness. He helped organise a university hackathon that drew more than 800 participants. Dheeraj values AI for speeding up development, but notes that convincing outputs can still be wrong; understanding fundamentals and critically reviewing generated solutions matter more than ever.</p>
          <p class="hot-take">🔥 The best engineers know what code shouldn't be written.</p>
        </article>

